## Tier by impact

| Preset | Impact | Complexity | Auto-detected? |
|--------|--------|------------|----------------|
| `shadcn` | High — most popular new pattern | Low | Yes (`@radix-ui/react-slot`) |
| `mui` | Critical — broken without it | High | Yes (`@mui/material`) |
| `chakra` | Critical — 200 style props without it | Medium | Yes (`@chakra-ui/react`) |
| `reactAria` | High — unique naming conventions | Medium | Yes (`react-aria-components`) |
| `mantine` | Medium — StylesApi noise | Low | Yes (`@mantine/core`) |
| `panda` | High — can't resolve RecipeVariants without styled-system | Medium | Yes (`panda.config.ts`) |
| `styledComponents` | Critical for those users — zero detection without it | High (extractor change) | Yes (`styled-components`) |
| `emotion` | Same as styled-components | High (extractor change) | Yes (`@emotion/react`) |

All Tier 1 should auto-activate. Explicit `presets: [...]` in config is the escape hatch for when you need different behavior than auto-detection gives you — disabling a preset, overriding its settings, or composing presets in a specific order.

