### Indexed access types — table lookup for known types

Rather than trying to resolve arbitrary `T["key"]` expressions (needs TSC), maintain a table of common known-type properties:

```rust
fn resolve_indexed_access(obj_type: &str, key: &str) -> Option<PropType> {
    match (obj_type, key) {
        ("CSSProperties" | "React.CSSProperties", _) => Some(PropType::String), // most CSS values
        ("CSSProperties" | "React.CSSProperties", "zIndex") => Some(PropType::Number),
        ("HTMLAttributes" | "React.HTMLAttributes", "className") => Some(PropType::String),
        ("HTMLAttributes" | "React.HTMLAttributes", "tabIndex") => Some(PropType::Number),
        ("HTMLAttributes" | "React.HTMLAttributes", "style") => Some(PropType::CssProperties),
        _ => None, // → Opaque { reason: IndexedAccess }
    }
}
```

